OL,3,GNEWSAArts worker unfairly dismissed
OL,4,Awhile facing cancer battle
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn arts charity unfairly dismissed a
OL,7,Fmember of staff who was undergoing
OL,8,Finvestigations for brain cancer, an
OL,9,Femployment tribunal has ruled.
OL,11,FBryan Peterson, who had worked for
OL,12,FShetland Arts Development Agency (Sada)
OL,13,Ffor 17 years, was going through a
OL,14,Fredundancy process when an MRI scan
OL,15,Findicated he likely had a life-limiting
OL,16,Ftumour.
OL,18,FPeterson asked for his redundancy to be
OL,19,Fpaused to allow for retirement due to
OL,20,Fill-health be explored instead, but the
OL,21,Fcharity refused the request.
OL,23,APub: 23-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
